  "notes": [
    "Services hosted at a branch are the ones whose front-end equipment is co-located there. Backend processing (CBS queries) always routes to HO.",
    "user_count is the number of customers actively served by that router at peak. Used for weighted health rollup.",
    "revenue_per_min_inr is the estimated loss if this router is fully down for 1 minute.",
    "branches_served counts branches that depend on this router for HO connectivity. HO serves 2 (both branches). ZO serves 2 (both branches). Branches serve only themselves.",
    "propagation is critical for RCA: a HO failure cascades to all routers. A ZO failure cascades to both branches. A branch failure is isolated."
